Australian Product Guide — Brand Fidelity v32.3 certified presentation release
Release date: 2026-08-18
Status: CURRENT / PRODUCTION VERIFIED / EXACT-SHA VISUAL CERTIFIED
Production source: GitHub main via Vercel
Canonical production domain: https://australianproductguide.au

Current platform: the underlying APG application/data capability remains the maintained priority-commerce / Decision Intelligence v4.1 / Evidence & Commerce Depth v27 / Trust Infrastructure v28 / Amazon Conversion v29 stack, with Premium Brand v30, Premium Theme v31.1 and Brand Fidelity v32.3 forming the current controlling presentation system. The architecture remains lightweight SSR-first Node with progressive enhancement. v32.3 changes presentation and release controls only; it does not change product-fit logic, catalogue data, retailer ranking, affiliate weighting, account/auth behaviour or privacy controls.

Brand-fidelity truth: the owner-approved APG brand board is implemented as a coherent production identity rather than an approximate A-shaped logo. The current mark uses the traced four-part APG geometry and first-party responsive assets for primary horizontal, compact, APG monogram, standalone symbol, white, monochrome, favicon, app-icon and social applications. Desktop uses the full Australian Product Guide lock-up. Standard tablet/mobile widths use the APG symbol/monogram relationship, with the monogram P kept white on navy so the complete APG mark remains legible.

Colour-system truth: the controlling palette is APG Blue #2563EB, APG Navy #0F172A, APG Teal #06B6D4, APG Green #10B981, Light Grey #F1F5F9 and Slate #64748B, supported by white and accessible light/dark text tokens. Navy is used for institutional authority and deep surfaces; blue is the primary action colour; teal/green remain selective accents; white/light grey provide breathing space. Dark surfaces use white or sufficiently light foreground text rather than low-contrast navy/grey combinations.

Maintained-research highlight: the successful historical yellow treatment was recovered from APG source history rather than guessed. The MAINTAINED AUSTRALIAN RESEARCH band uses #FFD65B → #F4BB45 → #F2B348, with #E0A630/#D89C24 border tones and dark foreground treatment. The main proof text remains based on the recovered #082735 family; v32.3 specifically forces the independence copy to #2B4B56 at strong weight after screenshot review found a too-light inherited legacy colour. Yellow remains a strategic trust accent rather than a primary site colour. The product/category/brand values remain data-driven from the authoritative maintained catalogue rather than hard-coded release numbers.

Scout and proof clearance: Scout remains APG's decision-assistance product and uses the APG Blue + white master symbol consistently after JavaScript initialisation. v32.2 introduced the runtime identity guard that prevents the legacy mascot overwriting the approved APG mark. v32.3 additionally makes the fixed desktop launcher a compact 58px APG-symbol control, preserving an explicit Ask Scout navigation entry and accessible launcher labelling while preventing the floating control from obscuring the yellow research independence statement. Scout decision logic, structured-session continuity and zero-commercial-weight recommendation controls are unchanged.

Catalogue and commerce snapshot at certification: live observability reported 482 maintained products, 90 populated categories and 178 canonical represented brands. Exact Australian retailer/manufacturer coverage was 52 verified destinations across 46 products from 20 sources, comprising 41 independent-retailer observations and 11 manufacturer-direct observations. The governed imagery registry still reports 0/482 verified external exact-model product photographs. Amazon Australia exact-identity readiness remains 22 products; transparent model-specific search fallbacks are used where exact Amazon identity is not verified. Affiliate participation, retailer availability and commission contribute zero recommendation points.

Imagery truth: APG continues to use first-party/category-correct authored decision visuals where authorised exact product photography is unavailable. APG does not scrape Amazon product pages, reverse-engineer image URLs, fabricate real-product photography or claim third-party imagery rights it does not hold. Authorised image delivery remains a separate ingestion task.

Responsive and accessibility truth: the final visual system has been inspected separately across desktop, tablet and mobile. It strengthens dark/light surface contrast, keeps the responsive APG monogram readable, preserves the distinctive yellow proof band, fixes the yellow-band independence-copy contrast, prevents true document-width overflow, retains readable footer/trust typography, and keeps product, comparison, search, Decision Lab, My APG and Scout surfaces visually coherent without turning the whole site dark. Legitimate internally scrollable comparison/research content is not incorrectly treated as page overflow.

Implementation and regression history: PR #79 established the v32.2 board-faithful identity and mobile/Scout corrections, with all 28 affected pull-request regression workflows passing. PR #80 reconciled the durable RELEASE record without changing runtime behaviour. Final screenshot review then identified two residual presentation defects in the yellow research band, so PR #81, Finish APG yellow proof contrast and Scout clearance, introduced Brand Fidelity v32.3. PR #81's 28 affected regression workflows all passed, including Brand Fidelity, Decision Intelligence, Amazon, retailer depth, platform integrity/cohesion, account/auth/governance, source, product-image, mobile and premium-theme controls.

Certified v32.3 runtime baseline: GitHub main implementation SHA a3ba69ad22d389abfb72f80ca75cb31f3bd403ee is a verified merge commit and was deployed as Vercel Production dpl_3Y17BpduiqFoqk1NipNMrVHg1vpP, READY in syd1 and aliased to australianproductguide.au. Canonical Production returned HTTP 200 with the v32.3 body marker and /assets/brand-fidelity-v323.css?v=32.3 layered after the v32.2/v32.1/v32 styles.

Exact-Production visual certification: APG v32 Brand Visual Certification run 32126838039 passed the exact-SHA deployment wait, v32.3 public-contract and Decision Lab SSR checks, desktop/tablet/mobile render matrix, current-main recheck and screenshot-artifact publication. The final artefact is 9320717339 (apg-v32-visual-32126838039), retained until 17 September 2026, with failures.json empty. APG v27 Visual Certification run 32126838057 also passed on the same v32.3 implementation SHA. Manual review of the final Production screenshots confirmed the board-faithful desktop/mobile identity, white responsive monogram P, APG-branded Scout, dark readable yellow-band independence copy, compact Scout clearance, product/comparison/Decision Lab surfaces and footer/trust treatments.

Remaining external gaps: lawful genuine-product photography ingestion remains incomplete until an authorised delivery/right basis exists. Hosted Supabase Auth settings outside the connected writable surface, including the previously identified leaked-password-protection setting, remain separate owner/admin configuration work unless subsequently verified otherwise. Formal trade mark clearance/registration is not claimed by this release.

Release discipline: GitHub main remains authoritative and Vercel Production must match it. The consumer-facing v32.3 runtime baseline certified above is a3ba69ad22d389abfb72f80ca75cb31f3bd403ee. This RELEASE-file reconciliation is documentation-only; its resulting main SHA must also receive a READY Production deployment and exact-commit visual certification before the operating-record reconciliation is closed.